`aplan add` scaffolds one task file. Its write path is covered against a temp tree in
`tests/add.rs`, and deliberately not here: a trycmd case that writes into its own `.in`
fixture leaves the file behind and the next run then sees a different plan. What is
pinned here is everything that does *not* write, which is where the guards live.

The id is derived from the convention the plan already uses, and `--dry-run` shows the
whole result without writing it. Both notes are the point of the command: it declines to
invent an estimate or a set of paths, and says what that will cost.

```
$ aplan add "Wire the sequencer" --dry-run
note: this adds 1 finding(s) `check` will report:
  APLAN009 A1-005: no `effort_days` estimate
      fix: Add an `effort_days` estimate, or drop the task.
would write A1-005  todo  Wire the sequencer
  -> aplan/tasks/A1-005.md
note: no `paths`; add them, or a commit cited later proves only that it exists (APLAN023)

```

Given what it cannot know, it stays quiet:

```
$ aplan add "Wire the sequencer" --dry-run --effort 2 --paths src/seq/**
would write A1-005  todo  Wire the sequencer
  -> aplan/tasks/A1-005.md

```

A milestone is a cut, not a task, so its id shape (`M-v0.1`) is never continued:

```
$ aplan add "Not a milestone" --dry-run --effort 1 --paths src/**
would write A1-005  todo  Not a milestone
  -> aplan/tasks/A1-005.md

```

An id that already exists is refused by id, not by path, because identity is the `id`
field:

```
$ aplan add "A clash" --id A1-004
? 2
aplan: task `A1-004` already exists in aplan/tasks/A1-004.md; refusing to overwrite it

```

A blocker that does not exist is refused before anything is written, rather than
producing a file `check` would reject:

```
$ aplan add "Bad blocker" --blocked-by A9-999
? 2
aplan: blocked by task(s) that do not exist: A9-999. `APLAN003` would reject the file, so the id is checked before the file is written.

```

A cut that is not a milestone is refused the same way `import --cut` refuses it:

```
$ aplan add "Wrong cut" --cut A1-004 --dry-run
? 2
aplan: `A1-004` is not tagged `milestone`, so it is not a cut

```
